          "en": "- **`if`**: no parentheses, braces are mandatory: `if port < 1024 { ... } else { ... }`.\n- **`for`** is the **only** loop in Go: `for i := 0; i < 3; i++ {}`, `for condition {}` (the\n  equivalent of `while`) and `for i, v := range list {}` to walk through a collection.\n- **`switch`**: no `break` to write, a `case` can list several values.\n- **Slice**: a dynamic list. `append(s, x)` adds, `len(s)` gives the size, `s[0]` reads an element.\n- **Map**: a key/value dictionary. `m[\"ssh\"] = 22` writes, `v, ok := m[\"ftp\"]` reads and tells you\n  whether the key exists. Map iteration order is **random**: sort the keys for a stable report.\n- **Function**: `func name(param type) returnType`. A function can return **several values**, and by\n  convention the last one is an `error`: `value, err := doSomething()`.\n\nThe `_` character (*blank identifier*) discards a value you do not need, for example the index in\n`for _, v := range list`.\n"
